/*
Strata's peer-review trainers: the visiting researchers (one per act), Theo Okafor's
peer reviews and Dr. Halvorsen's final one. Humans only battle in the present day, framed
as peer review: two people pit their reconstructions against each other.

Included by src/data.c after trainers.party (generated into src/data/trainers_strata.h by
trainerproc, see trainer_rules.mk). The trainer IDs are in include/constants/opponents.h.

Design (docs/strata_design.md, "Peer review"):
  - Teams are species the player has met by the act just finished (first_era of every species
    is at most that act: test/strata_review.c checks it), at levels between the next layer's era
    floor and the act's expected party level, so a party that finished the act can win. The last
    animal sets the prize: money is 4 x its level x the class multiplier (battle_main.c: 12 for
    the visiting researchers, 10 for Theo, 14 for Halvorsen).
  - IVs are 15 everywhere: the average of a wild catch, which balance.py uses.
  - No held items and no set moves: every animal uses the last four moves it learns by its level.
*/

/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* Theo Okafor, peer review #0 (present day, starter chosen): one animal at Lv 5, the starter */
/* after yours in the cycle mammal -> bird -> turtle -> mammal. Which trainer Theo is depends */
/* on VAR_STARTER_MON (data/maps/StrataFieldCamp/scripts.inc). */
/* --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

